From de90644e518edb36981f7b0dc31157e1b8f4bcd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkrze <mateusz.krzemieniewski@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:47:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add XPU support to the FBGEMM permute indices tests

Run sparse/permute_indices_test.py on the current accelerator through the
shared accelerator helpers: permute_1D_sparse_data and permute_2D_sparse_data
are compared against the CPU kernels on XPU, including non-contiguous inputs,
2D weights, vectorized remainders, large segments, preallocated outputs, the
scripted op and the backward pass. Import fbgemm_xpu to register the XPU
implementations.

Three large-grid tests stay CUDA/ROCm-only: permute_sparse_features has no
XPU kernel, and the permute_1D and permute_2D XPU kernels do not cap their
launch range yet, so these grids exceed the int range of a SYCL launch.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
